  "solution": {
    "text": "$I=\\int_0^{\\pi / 2} \\log \\left(\\frac{4+3 \\sin x}{4+3 \\cos x}\\right) d x$\n\nApplying King's property\n$I=\\int_0^{\\pi / 2} \\log \\left(\\frac{4+3 \\cos x}{4+3 \\sin x}\\right) d x$\n$\\begin{aligned} & 2 I=\\int_0^{\\pi / 2} \\log \\left(\\left(\\frac{4+3 \\sin x}{4+3 \\cos x}\\right)\\left(\\frac{4+3 \\cos x}{4+3 \\sin x}\\right)\\right) d x=0 \\\\ & I=0\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
